/F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 657 Tm (1. Summary) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 630 Tm (Gatekeeper is an RL environment for access-policy repair. The agent is given a) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 616 Tm (world model, a broken policy and a natural-language policy specification. It) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 602 Tm (uses a bounded tool interface to edit the policy, then submits it. A trusted) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 588 Tm (verifier evaluates the submitted policy over a hidden, exhaustive request) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 574 Tm (matrix. The core design question is not "can a model call tools?" but "can a) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 560 Tm (model reason about authorization semantics without overfitting visible examples) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 546 Tm (or leaking the answer key?") Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 527 Tm (The environment is deliberately model-agnostic: the harness speaks the) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 513 Tm (OpenAI chat-completions tool-call protocol, with a lenient fallback for models) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 499 Tm (that emit JSON in text. No model-specific prompting or fine-tuning is required.) Tj
/F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 472 Tm (2. Goals and non-goals) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 437 Tm (Goals) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 413 Tm (- A self-contained, deterministic task suite with easy, medium and hard tiers.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 399 Tm (- A hidden answer key and exhaustive scoring path that cannot be inspected by) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 385 Tm (  the agent.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 371 Tm (- Realistic authorization semantics: default deny, deny-overrides-allow,) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 357 Tm (  conditions, exceptions, nested groups and wildcards.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 343 Tm (- Strong baseline gates that catch trivial or broken environments.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 329 Tm (- A one-command Docker Compose workflow.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 315 Tm (- Useful trajectories and baseline artifacts for judging and debugging.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 301 Tm (- Clear failure modes: invalid config, crash, gate failure, model failure,) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 287 Tm (  step cap and wall-clock cap.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 260 Tm (Non-goals) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 236 Tm (- General-purpose IAM administration or production policy deployment.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 222 Tm (- Executing arbitrary code in the sandbox.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 208 Tm (- Hard guarantees against a malicious harness operator. The harness is trusted;) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 194 Tm (  the untrusted boundary is the model and its tool calls.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 180 Tm (- Training a model. The project supplies the environment and evaluation path.) Tj
