/F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 711 Tm (13. Risks and tradeoffs) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 684 Tm (- Generation cost. Full-matrix scoring for hard tasks and candidate mutation) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 670 Tm (  trials is expensive. The generator uses a fixed sample for mutation impact and) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 656 Tm (  a cache keyed by \(task_id, seed\). Hard tasks took roughly 8-20 seconds on) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 642 Tm (  first generation.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 628 Tm (- Deny-list shape. The protected allow-all baseline makes the correct policy) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 614 Tm (  less like a typical least-privilege policy. It is a deliberate anti-gaming) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 600 Tm (  tradeoff that guarantees allow-all and deny-all both fail.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 586 Tm (- Harness trust. The harness has model and oracle access. A malicious) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 572 Tm (  operator could leak answers; the design protects against model actions, not a) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 558 Tm (  malicious host.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 544 Tm (- Mock solver. The offline solver consumes oracle actions. It is useful for) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 530 Tm (  the gate/demo but is not evidence of model reasoning.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 516 Tm (- No code execution. The sandbox tools are declarative. This reduces risk but) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 52 502 Tm (  also limits the environment to policy-repair tasks.) Tj
